## Why

M5 establishes synchronous components, checked imports and independently bound
host rights; M6 separately completes its bounded native-async slice. Neither
delivers M7's scoped dataspace/facet semantics, Preserves service decoding or
executed two-participant service. Existing S-CASE-09 through S-CASE-12 and
WI-14 are unexecuted designs. M7 needs a concrete local synchronous contract
without promoting the selected concurrency direction to general Syndicate,
distributed delivery, durability or native-async acceptance.

## What Changes

- Select `Syndicate-Sync-Service-M7`: serialized facet-owned assertions and
  exact-pair interests, checked host-bound rights, replacement/retraction,
  recursive trap cleanup, finite state/event capacity and isolated participants.
- Define the canonical bounded Preserves text subset for
  `service(name:Text,ready:Bool)`, with strict schema, UTF-8, depth and byte
  checks and no payload-to-resource or payload-to-authority conversion.
- Select the versioned synchronous `noble:syndicate@1.0.0` `service` WIT world,
  including exact `(name,ready)` membership observation and compiled
  publish-then-trap; versioned import requests retain effects.
- Add positive S-CASE-17 and WI-18 designs requiring independently executed
  compiled Noble publisher/subscriber instances and real Preserves roundtrip.
  Extend S-CASE-09..12 and WI-14 negative designs against production
  boundaries; their execution remains not-run until evidence is retained.

## Impact

- **Files**: canonical `.cairn/specs/{safety,wit-wasi}/spec.md`, exact change
  deltas, conformance cases, generated compatibility views/ledger; separately
  owned production kernel/CLI/component WIT and future M7 execution evidence.
- **Testing**: actual Noble compilation, independently typed component peer,
  two separate component participants, true/false exact membership, local
  add/remove and post-trap retraction, bounded Preserves roundtrip and hostile
  adapter controls, wrong-right/shared-memory rejection, child/interest
  cleanup, complete declared quotas, separate source-bound assurance and
  earlier milestone regressions before any M7 closeout. A document check is
  not executable service evidence.
- **Non-goals**: full Syndicate/Synit, general Preserves, WASI, M6 native async,
  fairness, remote exactly-once effects, durability, choreography or universal
  runtime/compiler/engine refinement.
